  "scientific_interpretation": [
    "The LARE representation family remains strongly competitive on the prospectively transferred B14 fixed-water-table one-day laboratory, but the B01 minimum state requirement does not transfer.",
    "The B01 C4V one-day groundwater minimum R8 is falsified as a material-invariant rule: on B14 the transferred lower-zone R3 member already crosses both R2 and FMC at every preregistered checkpoint.",
    "Profile/process information remains more demanding. At day 1.024, R8 is the minimum reduced LARE member that also crosses FMC when mapped 10-cm theta RMSE is added, while R3 already crosses R2 on that profile-inclusive vector.",
    "Layer placement is decisive at fixed state count. R4 and the preregistered P4_TOP_LOWER both retain the groundwater frontier, while uniform U4 does not cross FMC; similarly R8 crosses both comparators while uniform U8 does not.",
    "Uniform U4/U8 failure despite the same nominal dimension confirms that state count cannot be interpreted independently from where vertical information is retained.",
    "B14 is one additional homogeneous material only. The result supports material-dependent state and placement requirements, not cross-material generality.",
    "No application acceptance, coupled-groundwater authority, portable speedup, timing claim or production ROM follows."
